  "note": "Sahana Mitra lives exclusively in tall-flats unit B and keeps a home-based tailoring trade; her rhythm is a late riser's and a late sewer's, unlike unit A's. Every day she sleeps 23:00-06:30, washes and dresses, cooks breakfast (07:00-07:30) and eats it (07:30-08:00). Monday to Friday she sews at home 08:00-12:30, takes a midday break until 13:15, readies herself, and leaves at 13:44 for an off-lane errand to a cloth and thread supplier, 14:00-15:30; she is back at 15:46, rests, and cooks supper from 16:30. On Saturday she sews 08:00-10:14, leaves for the same errand 10:30-12:00, is back at 12:16, breaks for a midday meal, sews again 13:00-15:00, rests and cooks from 16:30. On Sunday there is no errand and no sewing before evening: she is at home, reads, cooks a midday meal, and rests. Every evening she sees visitors about fittings 17:00-18:00, has supper 18:00-19:00, reads 19:00-20:30 and then does her late sewing 20:30-21:30 before resting until sleep. She is therefore home and Awake throughout the door's 17:00-20:30 visiting window all seven days; between 20:30 and 21:30 she is at her sewing and busy. Her home is off-lane behind the unit B door inside the shared passage; the visible 500 cm route ceiling joins its doorstep to the public front threshold, and the remaining 1680 cm errand route is off-lane. She never uses unit A. Travel is ceil(total route length / 140): 4 minutes doorstep to threshold, 12 minutes threshold to errand, 16 minutes each way in all.",
